  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.3.1 - Fixes, no API change:\n- A retrieve that returned no rows, called with a column-definition callback,\n  executed its command a second time to learn the result's shape. For a\n  procedure that writes, that repeated the write and discarded its result. The\n  shape now comes from the reader that already ran.\n- A connection scope's command-timeout override was written to the shared\n  provider, so it became the default for commands in other scopes until the\n  next connection opened. Each command keeps its own scope's override; the\n  provider's CommandTimeout is no longer changed by opening a connection.\n- The procedure parameter cache held a live view of the first command's\n  parameters, which kept that command reachable for the life of the process.\n  It now stores detached copies.\n- A reader no longer creates an unused SqlDataAdapter per call.\n- System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs, which arrives transitively, is pinned to\n  the patched release of its line (8.0.2; 9.0.22 on net10.0) to clear\n  GHSA-846f-f764-76mx and GHSA-2fmv-rv2c-59x7.\n\n1.3.0 - Adds a net10.0 target and drops net9.0 (end of support; a net9 consumer\nresolves the net8.0 assets). Requires CodexMicroORM.Core 1.4.1, which fixes a\npermanent ServiceScope leak - see that package's notes.\n\nNo API change. AssemblyVersion deliberately stays 1.2.0.0 so existing binding is\nunaffected on the net462 target.",
